        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Sing Out for Ireland\n- Organizations: The Wolfe Tones\n- People: Theobald Wolfe Tone\n- Events: Irish Rebellion of 1798\n- Concepts: Wolf tone\n\nFacts:\n- Theobald Wolfe Tone was an Irish rebel and patriot who was one of the leaders of the Irish Rebellion of 1798.\n- The Wolfe Tones take their name from Theobald Wolfe Tone.\n- The Wolfe Tones' name also uses a double entendre referring to a wolf tone, a spurious sound that can affect instruments of the violin family.\n- Sing Out for Ireland is the fourteenth album by the Irish folk and rebel band The Wolfe Tones.",
